{\pard \ql \f0 \sa180 \li0 \fi0 \outlinelevel0 \b \fs36 Item Envelope Manager\par}
{\pard \ql \f0 \sa180 \li0 \fi0 A compact non-destructive sound-design editor for Volume, Pitch, Pan, and Speed curves.\par}
{\pard \ql \f0 \sa180 \li0 \fi0 \outlinelevel1 \b \fs32 Workflow\par}
{\pard \ql \f0 \sa0 \li360 \fi-360 1.\tx360\tab Select audio items, drag one region, then Ctrl+drag to add more regions.\par}
{\pard \ql \f0 \sa0 \li360 \fi-360 2.\tx360\tab Choose Volume, Pitch, Pan, or Speed.\par}
{\pard \ql \f0 \sa0 \li360 \fi-360 3.\tx360\tab The current curve is previewed over that exact waveform region.\par}
{\pard \ql \f0 \sa0 \li360 \fi-360 4.\tx360\tab Edit points, Alt+drag a segment for curvature, or load a preset.\par}
{\pard \ql \f0 \sa0 \li360 \fi-360 5.\tx360\tab Open/close Volume, Pitch, and Pan envelopes without deleting their points.\par}
{\pard \ql \f0 \sa0 \li360 \fi-360 6.\tx360\tab Apply maps every representative range proportionally to all selected items.\par}
{\pard \ql \f0 \sa0 \li360 \fi-360 7.\tx360\tab Speed uses replaceable Preview Takes for safe A/B, Commit, and Original Restore.\sa180\par}
{\pard \ql \f0 \sa180 \li0 \fi0 \outlinelevel1 \b \fs32 Requirements\par}
{\pard \ql \f0 \sa0 \li360 \fi-360 \bullet \tx360\tab REAPER 7.0 or later\par}
{\pard \ql \f0 \sa0 \li360 \fi-360 \bullet \tx360\tab ReaImGui 0.9.2 or later\sa180\par}
{\pard \ql \f0 \sa180 \li0 \fi0 \outlinelevel1 \b \fs32 License\par}
{\pard \ql \f0 \sa180 \li0 \fi0 Copyright (c) 2026 Yoon-Soo Lee. All rights reserved. Redistribution, resale, or secondary distribution requires written permission.\par}
}

{\rtf1\ansi\deff0{\fonttbl{\f0 \fswiss Helvetica;}{\f1 \fmodern Courier;}}
